# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Service Reminder — contributor setup guide
#
# This file is a documentation template only; the app does NOT read it at
# runtime. Copy the relevant sections and follow the steps in README.md.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


# -- 1. Google Sign-In / Google Drive backup -----------------------------------
#
# Required for the optional Google Drive backup feature.
# Without it the app still runs fine — Settings just shows
# "Google Sign-In not set up" and the backup buttons are hidden.
#
# Steps:
#   a) Create (or reuse) a Firebase project at https://console.firebase.google.com
#   b) Enable the Google Drive API in Google Cloud Console.
#   c) Add an Android app with package name: com.servicereminder.service_reminder
#   d) Add your debug SHA-1 (run: keytool -list -v -keystore ~/.android/debug.keystore)
#      and your release SHA-1 (from your release keystore) to the Firebase app.
#   e) Download google-services.json and place it at:
#        android/app/google-services.json      <- gitignored, never commit this
#
# This file is gitignored. See README.md "Google Sign-In setup" for full details.


# -- 2. Release signing (Android) ---------------------------------------------
#
# Required only for Play Store / release builds. Debug builds work without it.
#
# Steps:
#   a) Generate a keystore (once ever — losing it means you can't update your
#      Play Store listing):
#        keytool -genkey -v `
#          -keystore /path/outside/repo/service-reminder-release.jks `
#          -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -alias service_reminder
#
#   b) Copy the template and fill in your values:
#        cp android/key.properties.example android/key.properties
#
#   c) Edit android/key.properties:
#
#        storePassword=YOUR_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
#        keyPassword=YOUR_KEY_PASSWORD
#        keyAlias=service_reminder
#        storeFile=/absolute/path/to/service-reminder-release.jks
#
# android/key.properties is gitignored — never commit it or your .jks file.


# -- 3. No other secrets required ---------------------------------------------
#
# All other config (app name, package ID, version, SDK versions) lives in
# pubspec.yaml and android/app/build.gradle.kts — both are committed.
